IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-s75-s79-officers.l4: sections 75 to 79 (disabilities of the Registrar and other officers; protection of the Registrar and other persons).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 4836-5014).
-- Answers seam 17 of PLAN.md with `s 79(2) the officer is not liable to be sued` (the asking section is s 65A(2), in scja2's range).
-- Where a section addresses an official only, it is encoded for what it decides; for the person (a suitor) it matters in ss 78 and 79.

§ `Sections 75 to 79: officers`

-- The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar and an Assistant Registrar: the persons ss 75 and 76 are about.
-- src:4840 | Disqualification of Registrar
-- src:4841 | 75.—(1) Except with the approval of the Chief Justice, the
-- src:4843 | Registrar, the Deputy Registrar and an Assistant Registrar —
@ref s 75(1) (the three Registrars) (src:4840-4843)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 75 the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` MEANS
    officer EQUALS Registrar OR officer EQUALS `Deputy Registrar` OR officer EQUALS `Assistant Registrar`

-- src:4841 | 75.—(1) Except with the approval of the Chief Justice, the
-- src:4843 | Registrar, the Deputy Registrar and an Assistant Registrar —
-- src:4844 | (a) shall not be capable of —
-- src:4845 | (i) accepting or taking any other office of emolument; or
-- src:4846 | (ii) carrying on any business either directly or indirectly;
-- src:4847 | and
-- src:4848 | (b) must not accept any fees of office, perquisites, emoluments
-- src:4849 | or advantages, other than his or her salary and allowances.
@ref s 75(1)(a)(i) (src:4841-4849)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
      `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(1)(a)(i) the officer is capable of accepting or taking any other office of emolument` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 75 the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` officer
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar and an Assistant Registrar"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the Chief Justice has approved`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "Except with the approval of the Chief Justice", and the text grants nothing where there is approval
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be capable of accepting or taking any other office of emolument"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

