-- src:4858 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the Registrar, the Deputy
-- src:4859 | Registrar and an Assistant Registrar may, with the approval of the
-- src:4860 | Chief Justice —
-- src:4862 | (a) be appointed to any commission of inquiry, committee of
-- src:4863 | inquiry or other judicial, quasi-judicial or administrative
-- src:4864 | tribunal, or hold any office in any institution or society for
-- src:4865 | charitable purposes or for the advancement or
-- src:4866 | encouragement of art, science, education or other
-- src:4867 | knowledge; and
-- src:4869 | (b) receive an allowance or other honorarium in respect of that
-- src:4870 | appointment or office.
@ref s 75(2) (src:4858-4870)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
      `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(2) the officer may be appointed to a commission or tribunal, hold office in a charitable or learned society, and receive an allowance or honorarium` MEANS
    IF `s 75 the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` officer AND `the Chief Justice has approved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is to the three Registrars "with the approval of the Chief Justice"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4876 | 76. The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar
-- src:4877 | must not, except with the approval of the Chief Justice, or with the
-- src:4878 | consent of the parties, investigate or hear and determine any
-- src:4879 | proceedings to or in which he or she is a party or personally
-- src:4880 | interested.
@ref s 76 (src:4876-4880)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
      `the officer is a party to or personally interested in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties have consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76 the officer may investigate or hear and determine the proceedings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 75 the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` officer
            AND `the officer is a party to or personally interested in the proceedings`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on the three Registrars, in "any proceedings to or in which he or she is a party or personally interested"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the Chief Justice has approved` OR `the parties have consented`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "except with the approval of the Chief Justice, or with the consent of the parties", and the text grants nothing where there is one
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not ... investigate or hear and determine any proceedings to or in which he or she is a party or personally interested"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4876 | 76. The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar
-- src:4877 | must not, except with the approval of the Chief Justice, or with the
-- src:4878 | consent of the parties, investigate or hear and determine any
-- src:4879 | proceedings to or in which he or she is a party or personally
-- src:4880 | interested.
@ref s 76 (the bar) (src:4876-4880)
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
      `the officer is a party to or personally interested in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties have consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76 the bar on investigating or hearing and determining the proceedings applies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 75 the officer is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` officer
            AND `the officer is a party to or personally interested in the proceedings`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on the three Registrars, in "any proceedings to or in which he or she is a party or personally interested"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the Chief Justice has approved` OR `the parties have consented`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is "except with the approval of the Chief Justice, or with the consent of the parties", so with either it does not apply (fork S3-B6)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The regulative twin of section 76: the Registrar shall not investigate or hear and determine the proceedings while the exceptions are not met.
-- Time is in abstract units; the number is the time at which the proceedings end.
DECLARE `s 76 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 76 the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar`

DECLARE `s 76 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76 investigates or hears and determines the proceedings`

-- src:4876 | 76. The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar
-- src:4877 | must not, except with the approval of the Chief Justice, or with the
-- src:4878 | consent of the parties, investigate or hear and determine any
-- src:4879 | proceedings to or in which he or she is a party or personally
-- src:4880 | interested.
@ref s 76 (the Registrar's duty) (src:4876-4880)
GIVEN `the officer is a party to or personally interested in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties have consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time at which the proceedings end` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 76 party` `s 76 act`
`s 76 the Registrar must not investigate or hear and determine proceedings in which the Registrar is interested` MEANS
    IF `the officer is a party to or personally interested in the proceedings` AND (NOT `the Chief Justice has approved`) AND (NOT `the parties have consented`)
    THEN PARTY `s 76 the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant Registrar`
         SHANT `s 76 investigates or hears and determines the proceedings`
         WITHIN `the time at which the proceedings end`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 76: the Registrar must not, except with the approval of the Chief Justice or with the consent of the parties, investigate or hear and determine proceedings in which he or she is a party or personally interested"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:4885 | 77. An officer of the Supreme Court having any duty to perform in
-- src:4886 | connection with the sale of any property under any written law must
-- src:4887 | not, directly or indirectly, purchase or bid for the property.
@ref s 77 (src:4885-4887)
GIVEN `the officer has a duty to perform in connection with the sale of the property under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77 the officer may purchase or bid for the property` MEANS
    IF `the officer has a duty to perform in connection with the sale of the property under a written law`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not, directly or indirectly, purchase or bid for the property"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "an officer of the Supreme Court having any duty to perform in connection with the sale of any property under any written law"
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 77 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 77 the officer of the Supreme Court`

DECLARE `s 77 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 77 purchases or bids for the property`

-- src:4885 | 77. An officer of the Supreme Court having any duty to perform in
-- src:4886 | connection with the sale of any property under any written law must
-- src:4887 | not, directly or indirectly, purchase or bid for the property.
@ref s 77 (the officer's duty) (src:4885-4887)
GIVEN `the officer has a duty to perform in connection with the sale of the property under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time at which the sale ends` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 77 party` `s 77 act`
`s 77 the officer must not purchase or bid for the property` MEANS
    IF `the officer has a duty to perform in connection with the sale of the property under a written law`
    THEN PARTY `s 77 the officer of the Supreme Court`
         SHANT `s 77 purchases or bids for the property`
         WITHIN `the time at which the sale ends`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BECAUSE "s 77: an officer of the Supreme Court having any duty to perform in connection with the sale of any property under any written law must not, directly or indirectly, purchase or bid for the property"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:4891 | 78.—(1) Without affecting any written law and rules governing the
-- src:4892 | conduct and discipline of public officers, if any officer of the
-- src:4893 | Supreme Court is charged —
-- src:4895 | (a) with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of
-- src:4896 | the process of the Supreme Court; or
-- src:4898 | (b) with not duly paying or accounting for any money levied
-- src:4899 | by the officer under the authority of this Act or Rules of
-- src:4900 | Court,
-- src:4907 | it is lawful for the Registrar to inquire into the matter in a summary
-- src:4908 | way.
@ref s 78(1) (src:4891-4908)
GIVEN `the officer is charged with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of the process of the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is charged with not duly paying or accounting for money levied under the authority of this Act or Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(1) it is lawful for the Registrar to inquire into the matter in a summary way` MEANS
    IF `the officer is charged with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of the process of the Supreme Court`
       OR `the officer is charged with not duly paying or accounting for money levied under the authority of this Act or Rules of Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if any officer of the Supreme Court is charged (a) with extortion or misconduct while acting under colour of the process of the Supreme Court; or (b) with not duly paying or accounting for any money levied"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4910 | (2) For the purpose of any such inquiry, the Registrar may summon
-- src:4911 | and enforce the attendance of all necessary parties in the like manner
-- src:4912 | as the attendance of witnesses in any case may be enforced.
@ref s 78(2) (src:4910-4912)
GIVEN `the Registrar is conducting an inquiry under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(2) the Registrar may summon and enforce the attendance of all necessary parties` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is conducting an inquiry under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "For the purpose of any such inquiry"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4914 | (3) On any such inquiry, the Registrar may make any order that the
-- src:4915 | Registrar thinks just for the repayment of the money extorted or the
-- src:4916 | due payment of the money levied, and for the payment of damages
-- src:4917 | and costs, and also, if the Registrar thinks fit, may impose a fine upon
-- src:4918 | the officer, not exceeding $100 for each offence, as appears to the
-- src:4919 | Registrar to be adequate.
@ref s 78(3) (the order) (src:4914-4919)
GIVEN `the Registrar is conducting an inquiry under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(3) the Registrar may order repayment of the money extorted, due payment of the money levied, and payment of damages and costs` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is conducting an inquiry under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "On any such inquiry"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4914 | (3) On any such inquiry, the Registrar may make any order that the
-- src:4915 | Registrar thinks just for the repayment of the money extorted or the
-- src:4916 | due payment of the money levied, and for the payment of damages
-- src:4917 | and costs, and also, if the Registrar thinks fit, may impose a fine upon
-- src:4918 | the officer, not exceeding $100 for each offence, as appears to the
-- src:4919 | Registrar to be adequate.
@ref s 78(3) (the fine) (src:4914-4919)
-- "not exceeding $100 for each offence" is the Act's own figure.
`s 78(3) the Act's maximum fine for each offence` MEANS 100

GIVEN `the Registrar is conducting an inquiry under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(3) the Registrar may impose a fine of that amount on the officer for the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar is conducting an inquiry under subsection (1)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "On any such inquiry"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the amount of the fine for the offence` AT MOST `s 78(3) the Act's maximum fine for each offence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may impose a fine upon the officer, not exceeding $100 for each offence"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4921 | (4) If it is found by the Registrar that any officer, while employed in
-- src:4922 | putting in execution this Act or Rules of Court or any of the powers
-- src:4923 | thereof, has wilfully and corruptly exacted or accepted any fee or
-- src:4924 | reward whatsoever (other than any fees that are for the time being
-- src:4925 | allowed under this Act or Rules of Court), that officer is, in addition
-- src:4926 | to being liable for damages under subsection (3), incapable of being
-- src:4927 | an officer of the Supreme Court.
@ref s 78(4) (src:4921-4927)
GIVEN `the Registrar has found that the officer, while employed in putting in execution this Act or Rules of Court or any of the powers thereof, wilfully and corruptly exacted or accepted a fee or reward` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee or reward was one allowed for the time being under this Act or Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(4) the officer is incapable of being an officer of the Supreme Court` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has found that the officer, while employed in putting in execution this Act or Rules of Court or any of the powers thereof, wilfully and corruptly exacted or accepted a fee or reward`
       AND NOT `the fee or reward was one allowed for the time being under this Act or Rules of Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it is found by the Registrar that any officer ... has wilfully and corruptly exacted or accepted any fee or reward whatsoever (other than any fees that are for the time being allowed under this Act or Rules of Court)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4929 | (5) An appeal lies to the Chief Justice from an order made by the
-- src:4930 | Registrar under this section.
@ref s 78(5) (src:4929-4930)
GIVEN `the order was made by the Registrar under section 78` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(5) an appeal lies to the Chief Justice` MEANS
    IF `the order was made by the Registrar under section 78`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the appeal lies "from an order made by the Registrar under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4932 | (6) The decision of the Chief Justice is final.
@ref s 78(6) (src:4932)
GIVEN `the decision is the Chief Justice's decision on an appeal under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(6) a further appeal lies from the decision of the Chief Justice` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the Chief Justice's decision on an appeal under subsection (5)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The decision of the Chief Justice is final."
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "the decision of the Chief Justice" on that appeal
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4940 | 79.—(1) The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar or an Assistant
-- src:4941 | Registrar or other person acting judicially shall not be liable to be
-- src:4942 | sued in any court exercising civil jurisdiction for any act done by him
-- src:4943 | or her in the discharge of his or her judicial duty whether or not within
-- src:4944 | the limits of his or her jurisdiction, provided that he or she at the time
-- src:4945 | in good faith believed himself or herself to have jurisdiction to do or
-- src:4946 | order the act complained of.
@ref s 79(1) (src:4940-4946)
GIVEN `the person is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or another person acting judicially` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was done in the discharge of the person's judicial duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person at the time in good faith believed himself or herself to have jurisdiction to do or order the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(1) the person is not liable to be sued in a court exercising civil jurisdiction for the act` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or another person acting judicially`
            AND `the act was done in the discharge of the person's judicial duty`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is for the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar "or other person acting judicially", for "any act done by him or her in the discharge of his or her judicial duty"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person at the time in good faith believed himself or herself to have jurisdiction to do or order the act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that he or she at the time in good faith believed himself or herself to have jurisdiction to do or order the act complained of"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4966 | (3) An officer of the Supreme Court is not to be deemed to have
-- src:4967 | acted knowingly in excess of his or her authority merely by reason of
-- src:4968 | the existence of a dispute as to the ownership of any property seized
-- src:4969 | under any enforcement order or writ of distress.
@ref s 79(3) (src:4966-4969)
GIVEN `the only ground for saying that the officer acted knowingly in excess of authority is a dispute as to the ownership of property seized under an enforcement order or writ of distress` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(3) the officer is deemed to have acted knowingly in excess of his or her authority` MEANS
    IF `the only ground for saying that the officer acted knowingly in excess of authority is a dispute as to the ownership of property seized under an enforcement order or writ of distress`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not to be deemed to have acted knowingly in excess of his or her authority merely by reason of the existence of a dispute as to the ownership of any property seized"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what the existence of a dispute does not do, and says nothing of any other ground
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4955 | (2) No officer of the Supreme Court charged with the duty of
-- src:4956 | executing any writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other
-- src:4957 | mandatory process of the court shall be liable to be sued in any
-- src:4958 | court exercising civil jurisdiction for the execution of or attempting to
-- src:4959 | execute such writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other
-- src:4960 | mandatory process, or in respect of any damage caused to any
-- src:4961 | property in effecting or attempting to effect execution, unless it
-- src:4962 | appears that he or she knowingly acted in excess of the authority
-- src:4963 | conferred upon him or her by such writ, summons, warrant, order,
-- src:4964 | notice or other mandatory process of the court.
@ref s 79(2) (src:4955-4964)
-- Seam 17 of PLAN.md.  JUST TRUE: the officer is not liable to be sued.  JUST FALSE: it appears that the officer knowingly acted in excess of the authority.
GIVEN `the officer is an officer of the Supreme Court charged with the duty of executing a writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is for the execution of or attempt to execute the process, or for damage to property in effecting or attempting to effect execution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that the officer knowingly acted in excess of the authority conferred by the process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only ground for saying that the officer acted knowingly in excess of authority is a dispute as to the ownership of property seized under an enforcement order or writ of distress` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(2) the officer is not liable to be sued` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the officer is an officer of the Supreme Court charged with the duty of executing a writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process of the court`
            AND `the claim is for the execution of or attempt to execute the process, or for damage to property in effecting or attempting to effect execution`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is for an officer "charged with the duty of executing" the process, "for the execution of or attempting to execute" it or for damage to property in doing so
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it appears that the officer knowingly acted in excess of the authority conferred by the process`
            AND NOT (`s 79(3) the officer is deemed to have acted knowingly in excess of his or her authority`
                       `the only ground for saying that the officer acted knowingly in excess of authority is a dispute as to the ownership of property seized under an enforcement order or writ of distress` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it appears that he or she knowingly acted in excess of the authority conferred upon him or her by such writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process of the court"
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4973 | (4) Where a registered medical practitioner, psychologist,
-- src:4974 | counsellor, social worker or mental health professional is appointed
-- src:4975 | by the General Division to examine and assess a child or person for
-- src:4976 | the purposes of preparing expert evidence for use in any proceedings
-- src:4977 | involving the custody or welfare of that child or involving that person
-- src:4978 | (as the case may be), the registered medical practitioner,
-- src:4979 | psychologist, counsellor, social worker or mental health
-- src:4980 | professional (as the case may be) shall not be liable to be sued for
-- src:4981 | an act done by him or her for the purposes of the examination or
-- src:4982 | assessment, or the preparation of the expert evidence for use in those
-- src:4983 | proceedings, if the act —
-- src:4985 | (a) was done in good faith; and
-- src:4987 | (b) did not involve any fraud or wilful misconduct on his or her
-- src:4988 | part.
@ref s 79(4) (src:4973-4988)
GIVEN `the professional was appointed by the General Division to examine and assess a child or person for the purposes of preparing expert evidence for use in proceedings involving the custody or welfare of the child or involving the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was done for the purposes of the examination or assessment, or the preparation of the expert evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was done in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act involved fraud or wilful misconduct on the professional's part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(4) the registered medical practitioner, psychologist, counsellor, social worker or mental health professional is not liable to be sued for the act` MEANS
    IF NOT `the professional was appointed by the General Division to examine and assess a child or person for the purposes of preparing expert evidence for use in proceedings involving the custody or welfare of the child or involving the person`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a registered medical practitioner, psychologist, counsellor, social worker or mental health professional is appointed by the General Division to examine and assess a child or person ...": the "Where" is unmet when the General Division did not appoint the professional (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05; fork S3-B3)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF NOT `the act was done for the purposes of the examination or assessment, or the preparation of the expert evidence`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is for "an act done by him or her for the purposes of the examination or assessment, or the preparation of the expert evidence", and the text says nothing of any other act
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF `the act was done in good faith` AND NOT `the act involved fraud or wilful misconduct on the professional's part`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the act (a) was done in good faith; and (b) did not involve any fraud or wilful misconduct on his or her part"
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4992 | (5) The Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a
-- src:4993 | court-appointed mediator is not liable to be sued for any act done by
-- src:4994 | him or her for the purposes of any mediation or other alternative
-- src:4995 | dispute resolution process conducted by him or her in the Supreme
-- src:4996 | Court, if the act —
-- src:4998 | (a) was done in good faith; and
-- src:5005 | (b) did not involve any fraud or wilful misconduct on his or her
-- src:5006 | part.
@ref s 79(5) (src:4992-5006)
GIVEN `the person is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a court-appointed mediator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was done for the purposes of a mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process conducted by the person in the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was done in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act involved fraud or wilful misconduct on the person's part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(5) the person is not liable to be sued for the act done for the purposes of the mediation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a court-appointed mediator`
            AND `the act was done for the purposes of a mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process conducted by the person in the Supreme Court`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the protection is for the Registrar, the Deputy Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a court-appointed mediator, for "any act done by him or her for the purposes of any mediation or other alternative dispute resolution process conducted by him or her in the Supreme Court"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the act was done in good faith` AND NOT `the act involved fraud or wilful misconduct on the person's part`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the act (a) was done in good faith; and (b) did not involve any fraud or wilful misconduct on his or her part"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5010 | (6) Any person or entity who does any act, or does not do any act, in
-- src:5011 | compliance with a prerogative order is immune from legal
-- src:5012 | proceedings in respect of that act or omission.
@ref s 79(6) (src:5010-5012)
GIVEN `the act or omission was in compliance with a prerogative order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(6) the person or entity is immune from legal proceedings in respect of the act or omission` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission was in compliance with a prerogative order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the immunity is for "any act, or does not do any act, in compliance with a prerogative order"
    ELSE NOTHING
